# Computation-side baseline handoff

This bundle was reconstructed on 2026-09-28 from the frozen three-draft **CM Structural Computation** research package created in the Master thread. It is intended to supply the computation-side materials that already exist here to the Computation thread and/or the convergence-audit thread.

## Important scope note

This is **not** a new Q_k Computation-thread milestone. It is the pre-existing computational baseline behind Draft 3, reorganized under the filenames requested by the new multi-thread protocol. In particular, the included tests do not directly verify the new Theory Phase 1 headline rank-threshold theorem unless a listed legacy test happens to overlap a special case. The Computation thread should still produce its own updated `HANDOFF_TO_MASTER.md`, `COMPUTATION_LEDGER.md`, and `EXPERIMENT_MANIFEST.csv` after completing the new Q_k work.

## Start here

1. `HANDOFF_TO_MASTER.md` - concise computation-side research handoff.
2. `COMPUTATION_LEDGER.md` - experiments, coverage, findings, and limitations.
3. `EXPERIMENT_MANIFEST.csv` - machine-readable experiment map.
4. `REPRODUCTION_COMMANDS.md` - exact replay commands.
5. `ENVIRONMENT.md` - recorded environment/version information.
6. `reproducibility/` - code, tests, raw results, data, logs, environments, version snapshots, and selected witnesses.
7. `historical_source_material/recovered_source/` - legacy source required by the clean replay.
8. `research/experiment_design/` - frozen experiment protocols, including the v3 timing replay protocol.
9. `manuscript_context/` - final Draft 3 TeX/PDF and claim crosswalk.

The authoritative detailed replay guide is also preserved verbatim at `reproducibility/README.md`.
